ui_readline: exit when stdin closes, if PIANOBAR_EXIT_ON_EOF is set.

PowerBar drives pianobar through a pipe on stdin. If the app goes away
without saying "q" (crash, force quit), the pipe closes and pianobar would keep
playing with nothing to control it. With the variable set, EOF on stdin quits.
Without it, behaviour is unchanged.

--- a/src/ui_readline.c	2026-11-22 21:24:52.000000000 -0700
+++ b/src/ui_readline.c	2026-11-22 21:24:52.000000000 -0700
@@ -104,6 +104,10 @@
 			 * available
 			 * FIXME: ugly */
 			if (curFd == STDIN_FILENO) {
+				if (getenv ("PIANOBAR_EXIT_ON_EOF") != NULL) {
+					/* our controlling app is gone */
+					exit (0);
+				}
 				FD_CLR (curFd, &input->set);
 			}
 			continue;
